\f1\fs26 The riots cops opened the forward port and starboard cabin doors as the pilot lowered the cruiser over the crush in the street. Pistols withdrew from holsters and aimed.\
\'93Take out only enough to get them moving,\'94 Corporal Sman ordered. \'93I don\'92t want to be here all night balancing the books.\'94\
Corporal Sman\'92s colleagues, who often accused him of pleasuring himself to pivot tables (they didn\'92t know what they were), promptly emptied their clips into the crowd of gawkers. Sman swore.\
The reaction was instant. Cries and screams went up as ripples in the crowd, like snakes under a rug, swelled one way then another. Eventually most of the crowd voted with their stamping feet to run away from the bomb site, and a grisly crop circle of trampled bodies bloomed under the cruiser.\
The co-pilot set the cruiser down and all the riots cops except Sman jumped out, who parked his butt in the port doorway and dangled his legs out. The cruiser rose again.\
\'93We need the right demographic spread of terrorists. Make sure you stick to the profiles I specified,\'94 Sman ordered as he practiced his aim.\
\'93Roger that,\'94 the lead cop answered.\
Alexander came and stood by Sman, and grabbed the doorway to keep balance as the cruiser slowly rotated. \'93How many more do you have to take out?\'94\
Sman threw a panoramic hologram into the air outside the cruiser, where it would be easy for him to monitor. Statistical tables scrolled, charts and graphs materialised, and faces appeared one after the other. \'93More than I\'92d like,\'94 he answered, aimed and shot into the crowd. A face popped up on his hologram with a green tick animating over it.\
\'93So I\'92m just here to endorse the culling and the bystanders you\'92ve nominated to play terrorist,\'94 Alexander said sullenly. It was not that he objected to the killing; it galled that he was not in charge of it.\
Sman took another shot. The hologram produced another face and another green tick.\
The cops punched through the crowd, looking for arrests that matched their profiles. The cruiser lazily rotated as Sman found targets and fired. On his hologram, a graph showed a series of lines that seems to be converging, and a pair of pie charts that were nearing becoming exact copies.\
Suddenly, the graphs lost their cohesion. Sman swore. \'93What\'92s going on down there?\'94 he demanded.\
\'93We\'92ve had some Resist Arrests,\'94 the lead cop reported. \'93Kramer shot a banker.\'94\
Sman was furious. \'93Do you know how rare a Cloudborne banker is? Now the demographic analysis looks like the banker was our sole intended target! I\'92ll have to start over.\'94 Sman twiddled and punched at the hologram and the whole of its panorama refreshed. Sman took aim and smiled at something in his scope. \'93Ah! White hip hop artist!\'94 He pulled the trigger.\
\'93They\'92re a demographic here?\'94 Alexander asked.\
\'93Not exactly. You can never take out too many white hip hop artists.\'94\
\'93Aren\'92t you endangering the demographic balance of the whole operation.\'94\
\'93Nah,\'94 Sman said as he popped more targets and earned more green ticks. \'93Community service. See?\'94 He paused and pointed to a floating graph. \'93Even the demographics don\'92t care.\'94\
\'93All targets acquired,\'94 the lead cop reported.\
The pilot landed the cruiser. The cops loaded a restrained, gagged and blindfolded mess of terrorists into the cargo hold, and boarded the cruiser.\
Once in the air, Sman resumed shooting.\
\'93Almost there?\'94 the lead cop quizzed him.\
Sman shot a few times then consulted his charts and graphs. \'93Pretty much, yeah. I could do with one more, just to be safe. Have pilot hover over the blast site.\'94\
\'93What are you looking for?\'94 Alexander asked, hoping he could be helpful, so he could tells his friends later, his contribution was the clincher.\
\'93I need an average Joe, preferably one of the bomb victims. White, thirties, manual labourer \'85 you know, a gardener or a cleaner or something.\'94 Sman scrolled through the casualty reports. the hologram went 
\f3\i bing
\f1\i0  and produced a face.\
To Alexander\'92s horror, it was Cracker\'92s. Jesus, they\'92d only been chatting last night, when Alexander called him in to clean up that suicide mess. With wide, panicked eyes, he scoured the blast zone for any sign of his \'85 well, not a friend exactly\'97Cracker was Cloudborne, after all\'97more a compatriot in a loosely acquainted (had a beer with him once or twice), kind of way.\
That\'92s when Alexander saw her. She was lying dead or unconscious in street, black and grey, cut and bruised. The way she lay was mesmerising. The flow of her long ashen hair spoke of the pure blonde beneath the caking dust. The soot could not disguise the architecture of her cheek bone, nor the artistry of the shape of her lips. Even her body lying at a misshapen angles could not disguise the elegance of her legs, the suppleness of her hips, the promise of her breasts.\
Choirs of angels sang to Alexander, and he fell in love.\
